From 53e5fc708db6b9d7bcb62054da67667f825e1617 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 08:54:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] perf(dsv41): size the WO and COMP L2 prefetch windows by row
 band

Upstream base: local-inference-lab/vllm 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354
with candidate-55's series applied through 0805.

Rationale:
The WO window (this layer's WO-A and WO-B weights; COMP in an owner layer takes
the same budget) fills while the sparse-MLA preparation kernels run. What the
fill costs those kernels grows with the rows; what it saves the projections
does not. One budget for every row count is therefore wrong somewhere: at TP4
on four GB10s with 15/12/12 MB, candidate-55 is 1.5-1.9% slower than
candidate-54 at the four 24-row grid shapes and 1.3% at 16x32, and not slower
with the prefetch off. With WO at 10 MB those shapes are 2.4-2.7% and 1.5%
faster, 1x2 rows 1.9% slower and 48-72 rows 0.5-1.6% slower
(spark-ds41f experiments/2026-10-26-spark-ds41f-candidate/candidate-55/
rows24-attribution). 24 and 32 rows are the 32-row decode tile tier.

VLLM_DS41_L2_PREFETCH_WO_BANDS names budgets by row count
("17-32=10": megabytes for forwards of 17 to 32 rows). build_l2_prefetch makes
one plan per band beside the default, and issue() launches the plan the
forward's row count selects. Under capture that choice is made once per graph,
so each captured row count replays its own plan; nothing is decided at replay.
Unset, make_wo_plan returns make_plan's plan itself and nothing changes. A
malformed value stops the worker at import.

Quality implications:
None. The windows are cache hints (createpolicy and bulk L2 prefetch only);
no kernel, launch order or arithmetic changes.

Tests:
- tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_l2_schedule.py: the parser, the plan without
  bands, the plan a row count selects, and issue() launching it (17 passed in
  the candidate-55 image on a GB10, pytest --noconftest).
- Mounted over candidate-55's fourth build with "17-32=10" at tp4-ring and
  tp4-switched, two boots each: the four 24-row grid shapes 2.70% and 2.23%
  faster, 16x32 1.70% and 2.10%, no other shape or the drafter moved, the grid
  0.45% and 0.52% faster, and the temperature-0 gate identical with
  candidate-54's hashes (spark-ds41f
  experiments/2026-11-13-l2-prefetch-row-bands).

Upstream status: local spark-ds41f patch, carried from candidate-55's fifth
build; not submitted upstream. Inert unless VLLM_DS41_L2_PREFETCH_WO_BANDS is
set.
